menu "HID remote"

    config BADGE_SHORTCUTS
        string "Shortcuts (semicolon separated, 19 characters each, 32 max; empty = no Shortcuts app)"
        default ""
        help
            One-press Home Assistant macros shown first on the main menu. Shortcut n sends a BTHome dimmer
            event rotate_right with steps = 200 + n; one HA automation per badge maps each number to a script
            (ha/wrench_shortcuts.yaml). Append new shortcuts at the end so numbers keep their meaning.

    config BADGE_MENU
        string "Home Assistant menu rows (semicolon separated, 19 characters each, 32 rows max)"
        default "Lights on;Lights off;Strip|Off|Rainbow|Fire;Blinds up;Blinds down;Good night"
        help
            Rows of the HA Menu app. Picking row r broadcasts a BTHome dimmer event rotate_right with steps = r
            (and the row text as sensor.<badge>_text, for the logbook). A row written as "Label|A|B|C" opens a
            popup of entries instead; entry k of row r sends rotate_left with steps = r*10+k (rows 1-24, up to
            9 entries). Automations key on those numbers (ha/wrench_menu_command.yaml), so append new rows and
            entries at the end. Texts are cut to 19 characters.

endmenu
